% The gate is guaranteed to open infinitely often.
%
% - this is not true for the model the guidelines request.
% - since the gate should remain open until there are no trains waiting,
% if trains keep comming and queue never empties, the gate remains open,
% therefore does not open infinitely often.
%
% We present a counterexample:
% t1 and t2 keep re-approaching, so the queue never empties.
[ approach(t1) . approach(t2)            % t1 and t2 are both waiting
  . (!up)* . leave(t1) . approach(t1)    % t1 crosses and queues again
  . (!up)* . leave(t2) . approach(t2)    % t2 crosses and queues again
] false
